  <section class="training-section" id="training-programmes" aria-labelledby="training-programmes-title">
    <div class="training-shell">
      <div class="training-section-heading">
        <p class="training-eyebrow training-eyebrow--dark">Certificate Programme</p>
        <h2 id="training-programmes-title">Advanced Vascular Intervention Training</h2>
        <p>Explore the two paid professional medical education programmes currently presented by Bankers Vascular Centre.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="training-program-card training-program-card--dark" id="gae-training" aria-labelledby="gae-training-title">
        <div class="training-program-copy">
          <p class="training-card-label">Programme 01</p>
          <h2 id="gae-training-title">Genicular Artery Embolization (GAE) Training for Doctors in India</h2>
          <h3>Advanced GAE Training with Live Clinical Case Exposure</h3>
          <p class="training-price">₹4,00,000 <span>— One-Time</span></p>
          <p>Genicular Artery Embolization (GAE) is a minimally invasive, image-guided technique involving selective embolization of abnormal vascularity associated with symptomatic knee osteoarthritis in appropriately selected patients.</p>
          <p>Doctors interested in developing their understanding of GAE can explore a structured training programme at Bankers Vascular Centre. Led by Dr. Mohal Banker and Dr. Rozil Gandhi, the programme combines theoretical education with practical learning and exposure to live clinical cases.</p>
          <a class="training-button training-button--light" href="#training-enquiry">Enquire About GAE Training</a>
        </div>
        <div class="training-program-details">
          <h3>GAE Training Programme Features</h3>
          <ul class="training-check-list">
            <li>Two training modules</li>
            <li>Theoretical learning</li>
            <li>10+ live training cases</li>
            <li>Hands-on experience</li>
            <li>Training by Dr. Mohal Banker and Dr. Rozil Gandhi</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="training-detail-block">
            <h3>Clinical Learning Focus</h3>
            <p>Relevant educational topics may include knee vascular anatomy, clinical indications, patient selection, diagnostic imaging, procedural planning, treatment principles and post-procedure assessment.</p>
            <p>The exact course curriculum and level of practical involvement must be confirmed with the training team.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="training-detail-block">
            <h3>Who May Be Interested?</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Interventional radiologists</li>
              <li>Radiologists pursuing interventional training</li>
              <li>Appropriately qualified specialists interested in image-guided embolization</li>
              <li>Medical professionals with relevant prior training seeking further clinical exposure</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Enrollment and participation in hands-on clinical activities depend on professional qualifications and applicable institutional requirements.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="training-supporting-text">Contact the training team to confirm programme duration, batch availability, eligibility, detailed syllabus and fee inclusions.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="training-program-card training-program-card--light" id="varicose-training" aria-labelledby="varicose-training-title">
        <div class="training-program-copy">
          <p class="training-card-label">Programme 02</p>
          <h2 id="varicose-training-title">Varicose Veins Treatment Training for Doctors in India</h2>
          <h3>Learn Contemporary Minimally Invasive Varicose Vein Management</h3>
          <p class="training-price">Starting From ₹2,00,000</p>
          <p>Varicose veins and chronic venous insufficiency are common vascular conditions requiring appropriate clinical evaluation and individualized treatment planning.</p>
          <p>Modern treatment approaches for eligible patients may include endovenous laser therapy, radiofrequency ablation, medical adhesive closure and other vein-directed interventions.</p>
          <p>Bankers Vascular Centre offers a professional Varicose Veins Treatment Training Programme for doctors interested in developing their knowledge of contemporary venous disease management.</p>
          <a class="training-button training-button--solid" href="#training-enquiry">Enquire About Varicose Veins Training</a>
        </div>
        <div class="training-program-details">
          <h3>Programme Highlights</h3>
          <ul class="training-check-list">
            <li>Five theoretical training modules</li>
            <li>Online course option available</li>
            <li>Hands-on experience</li>
            <li>Personalized training</li>
            <li>Learning with Dr. Mohal Banker and Dr. Rozil Gandhi</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="training-detail-block">
            <h3>Clinical Learning Focus</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Understanding varicose vein disease and chronic venous insufficiency</li>
              <li>Patient assessment and Duplex Doppler ultrasound evaluation</li>
              <li>Principles of minimally invasive venous treatment</li>
              <li>Endovenous treatment approaches</li>
              <li>Patient selection, treatment planning, safety and follow-up</li>
            </ul>
            <p>These are suggested learning areas, not a confirmed list of course modules. Only label them as included curriculum after verification.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="training-detail-block">
            <h3>Personalized Learning Approach</h3>
            <p>Doctors enter training with different levels of experience in vascular imaging and interventional procedures. Our personalized training approach allows participants to discuss their learning requirements and explore suitable educational opportunities.</p>
            <p>An online course option is available for the Varicose Veins Training Programme. Contact the team for the exact division between theoretical and practical training.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="training-supporting-text">Request information about admission, course structure, hands-on training, online learning and available schedules.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

