  <section class="training-section training-faq-section" aria-labelledby="training-faq-title">
    <div class="training-shell training-faq-grid">
      <div class="training-section-heading">
        <p class="training-eyebrow training-eyebrow--dark">Doctor-specific FAQ</p>
        <h2 id="training-faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions About GAE and Varicose Veins Training</h2>
        <p>These answers summarise currently published programme information. Confirm the latest arrangements with the training team.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="training-faq-list">
        <details><summary>Where can doctors learn Genicular Artery Embolization in India?</summary><p>Bankers Vascular Centre offers a Genicular Artery Embolization training programme led by Dr. Mohal Banker and Dr. Rozil Gandhi. The programme includes theoretical learning, 10+ live training cases and hands-on experience.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the fee for Genicular Artery Embolization training?</summary><p>The published GAE training fee is ₹4,00,000 as a one-time payment. Contact the training team for fee inclusions and enrollment details.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is hands-on GAE training available?</summary><p>Yes. Hands-on experience is included in the published programme features. Actual clinical participation depends on qualifications, supervision, patient consent and institutional requirements.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the fee for Varicose Veins Treatment Training?</summary><p>The Varicose Veins Treatment Training Programme starts from ₹2,00,000. Contact the team to confirm available training options and pricing.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is online Varicose Veins Training available?</summary><p>Yes. An online course option is available. Doctors can enquire about the programme structure and practical learning arrangements.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Who conducts the training programmes?</summary><p>The listed trainers are Dr. Mohal Banker and Dr. Rozil Gandhi, interventional radiologists associated with Bankers Vascular Centre.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How many live cases are included in GAE training?</summary><p>The programme lists exposure to 10+ live training cases. Case availability and participation arrangements should be confirmed before enrolling.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does the GAE or Varicose Veins Training Programme take?</summary><p>The exact duration is not currently published. Contact the training coordinator for the latest schedule and programme duration.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Who is eligible for these medical training programmes?</summary><p>These programmes are intended for appropriately qualified medical professionals. Eligibility and permitted hands-on participation depend on prior training, clinical competence and institutional requirements.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is a training certificate provided?</summary><p>The programmes are advertised under a Certificate Programme section. Participants should confirm certificate details, completion requirements and any applicable recognition with the training team.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How can doctors register for training?</summary><p>Doctors can contact Bankers Vascular Centre using the enquiry options on this training page or the published contact details.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

